From 2d2e1bcb4c2bf951b2f220b1d888026f4bc69e53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 04:39:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Fix cursor tool_choice handling, tool-call usage
 reporting, and session/cache affinity

- tool_choice was dropped in the OpenAI->cursor request conversion: parse
  string and object forms (auto/none/required/any and forced function,
  including Claude-style {type:tool}), narrow the advertised tool set, and
  inject an explicit system directive since Agent Connect has no native
  tool_choice field. Warn when a forced tool call is not satisfied.
- Responses with tool_calls reported usage.prompt_tokens=0: TurnEnded arriving
  while client tools are pending had its token counts discarded. Emit the
  usage event before segment_end and swallow the stale pre-tool TurnEnded
  after a resume so it cannot prematurely end the next segment.
- Surface cached/reasoning token details in non-stream usage and emit a final
  usage chunk on streamed responses.
- Pin tool-result continuation requests to the auth that owns the live Cursor
  session (sticky auth hint consulted by all selectors) so account rotation
  cannot break the session or throw away the provider prompt cache.
- Rebuild the run from full history (including trailing tool results) when the
  live bidi stream died while waiting for tool results, instead of failing
  the request.

Co-authored-by: Apologetic2022 <Apologetic2022@users.noreply.github.com>
